  "reasoning": "This commit (\"migrating to SConcept in typesystem rules (isApplicable): runtime\") changed the `getParents` method in RuleSet.java from using `getConceptDescriptor(nextConceptFQName).getParentsNames()` (direct parents only) to `SConceptOperations.getAllSuperConcepts(nextConcept, false)` (all ancestor concepts, not just direct ones). Since `SingleTermRules.computeRules` already performs a BFS/queue-based traversal calling `getParents` recursively to walk up the concept hierarchy, using `getAllSuperConcepts` instead of `getDirectSuperConcepts` caused incorrect/excessive concept matching in the type system rule engine, leading to the described type error for code like `a+='d'`. The fix simply restores the correct direct-parents-only semantics by switching to `getDirectSuperConcepts`.",
